tstrap_become\' and \'bootstrap_become_user\' are used where necessary. Also, each task should have the appropriate \'become\' and \'become_user\' settings if required.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I\'ll structure each task under the \'tasks\' key in YAML, making sure each task is properly indented and follows the correct syntax. I\'ll avoid adding any comments or explanations, just the YAML code as required.\n\nI should double-check each task to ensure that the module names, parameters, and structure match the user\'s instructions precisely. For example, Task 3\'s raw command should execute the package script and register the result to check for changes.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the playbook starts with \'---\' and that there are no extra lines or formatting issues. This should meet all the user\'s requirements and fit seamlessly into an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Assert Variables\n  include_tasks: assert.yml\n  register: assert_result\n  remote_host: localhost\n\n- name: Wait for Host\n  wait_for_host:\n    state: started\n    port: 22\n    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout }}"\n  when:\n    - not (ansible_connection == \'docker\' or ansible_connection == \'container\')\n    - bootstrap_wait_for_host\n\n- name: Prepare System\n  block:\n    - name: Test connection\n      ping:\n        remote_host: "{{ inventory_hostname }}"\n      ignore_errors: yes\n      register: connection_test\n\n    - name: Debug connection failure\n      debug:\n        msg: "Could not connect to host"\n      when: connection_test.failed\n\n    - name: Gather bootstrap facts\n      gather_facts:\n        facts_file: "bootstrap_facts.json"\n\n    - name: Install bootstrap packages\n      raw: "{{ bootstrap_package_install_cmd }}"\n      register: bootstrap_packages_installed\n      changed_when: bootstrap_packages_installed.stdout != \'\'\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  become: "{{ bootstrap_become }}"\n  become_user: "{{ bootstrap_become_user }}"\n\n- name: Ensure Sy