rs are notified: \'Test httpd configuration validity\' and \'Restart httpd\'.\n\nI\'ll use the \'template\' module to generate the config file. The \'notify\' attribute will trigger the handlers. I need to make sure the template file exists in the correct path relative to the role\'s structure.\n\nI should also define the handlers in the playbook. \'Test httpd configuration validity\' can run \'apache2ctl configtest\', and \'Restart httpd\' will restart Apache.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure the tasks with the appropriate conditions and notifications. I\'ll ensure that the YAML is correctly formatted, using the correct indentation and structure for blocks and tasks.\n\nI need to avoid adding any hosts, vars, or playbook-level headers, as per the user\'s instructions. Only the tasks and handlers should be included.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure it starts with \'---\', includes both tasks with the correct modules and handlers, and adheres to all the specified requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable modules\n  block:\n    - name: Enable proxy module\n      apt:\n        name: proxy\n        state: present\n        enable: true\n      when: ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']\n    - name: Enable proxy_http module\n      apt:\n        name: proxy_http\n        state: present\n        enable: true\n      when: ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'ubuntu\']\n    - name: Enable proxy module on Suse\n      shell: a2mavctl --enable proxy\n      when: ansible_distribution == \'suse\'\n    - name: Enable proxy_http module on Suse\n      shell: a2mavctl --enable proxy_http\n      when: ansible_distribution == \'suse\'\n  notify: Reload Apache\n\n- name: Configure locations\n  template:\n    src: httpd_locations.conf.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_directory }}/httpd_locations.conf"\n    owner: www-data\n    group: www-data\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: \n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n```