tlining each task with the correct modules and parameters. For Task 3, I\'ll break it into a pre_task and the main copy task because the source depends on the result of the pre_task.\n\nWait, but in Ansible, pre_tasks run before any tasks in the role, so I can use a separate pre_tasks section. But since the user specified tasks exactly as described, maybe I should handle it within the same tasks list. Alternatively, I can include the pre_task within the same tasks but ordered before the main task.\n\nI think the pre_task approach is better. So, I\'ll create a pre_task that checks the file\'s existence and permissions, sets a variable, and then use that variable in the main copy task.\n\nI should also ensure that the file is copied only if it doesn\'t exist or if the conditions are met. So, the copy task should have the remote_src set to True if needed, but I think the copy module doesn\'t require that. Wait, no, the copy module\'s remote_src is for copying from another host, which isn\'t the case here.\n\nI\'ll set the source based on the variable determined in the pre_task.\n\nAfter copying, I need to notify the handler, so I\'ll add notify: \'Restart systemd-sysctl\' to the copy task.\n\nFinally, for Task 4, I\'ll use the meta module to flush handlers.\n\nI need to make sure all tasks are correctly ordered and that variables are properly passed.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll write each task with the correct module and parameters, ensuring that the playbook starts with \'---\' and only contains valid YAML for tasks.\n\nI should also check for any typos and ensure that the YAML syntax is correct, as per yamllint and ansible-lint standards.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create etcd group\n  group:\n    name: etcd\n    state: present\n    system: true\n\n- name: Create etcd user\n  user:\n    name: etcd\n    shell: /bin/nologin\n    group: etcd\n    comment: etcd user\n    state: present\n\n- name: Check if /usr/local/share/rke2/rke2-cis-sysctl.conf is presen