content='<think>\nAlright, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given instructions. Let me go through each step carefully.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the very first line. I\'ll make sure that\'s the opening.\n\nNext, I\'ll structure the tasks as described, keeping the order exactly as specified. Each task has a specific name and description, so I\'ll ensure I don\'t miss any.\n\nTask 1 is to import assert.yml from localhost and run it once. I\'ll use the import_tasks module with remote_src set to true and the no_cache option.\n\nTask 2 installs MySQL using the package manager. The variable \'mysql_packages\' holds the package names. After installation, it notifies two handlers: \'Set root password\' and \'Systemctl daemon-reexec\'.\n\nTask 3 configures the MySQL server by modifying the config file. It uses the variable \'mysql_configuration_options\' and notifies \'Restart mysql server\' after each change.\n\nTask 4 configures the MySQL client, setting the socket option to \'mysql_socket\'. This is a simple template or command to update the client config.\n\nTask 5 initializes MySQL only for Alpine or Archlinux. I\'ll use a shell command from \'mysql_initialize_command\' and conditionally run it based on the distribution.\n\nTask 6 starts and enables the MySQL service using systemctl. The service name comes from \'mysql_service\'.\n\nTask 7 flushes handlers to run any notified tasks immediately.\n\nTask 8 places my.cnf using a template, setting the correct mode.\n\nTask 9 creates databases if \'mysql_databases\' is defined. It uses MySQL authentication variables.\n\nTask 10 creates users similarly, based on \'mysql_users\'.\n\nTask 11 flushes handlers again to ensure all changes are applied.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the correct module, arguments, and notify handlers. I\'ll also include conditionals where necessary, like for Tasks 5, 9, and 10.\n\nFinally, I\'ll ensure the YAML is valid, adhering to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. The playbook should be self-contained and ready to include in an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  remote_src: true\n  no_cache: yes\n\n- name: Task 2: Install mysql\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ mysql_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  notify:\n    - Set root password\n    - Systemctl daemon-reexec\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure mysql server\n  template:\n    src: mysql-server.cnf.j2\n    dest: "{{ mysql_configuration_destination }}/mysql-server.cnf"\n  notify: Restart mysql server\n\n- name: Task 4: Configure mysql client\n  template:\n    src: mysql-client.cnf.j2\n    dest: "{{ mysql_configuration_destination }}/mysql-client.cnf"\n  vars:\n    socket: "{{ mysql_socket }}"\n\n- name: Task 5: Initialize mysql\n  shell: "{{ mysql_initialize_command }}"\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  when: ansible_distribution in [\'Alpine\', \'Archlinux\']\n\n- name: Task 6: Start and enable mysql\n  systemctl:\n    name: "{{ mysql_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Task 7: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Task 8: Place my.cnf\n  template:\n    src: my.cnf.j2\n    dest: /etc/my.cnf\n    mode: 0640\n\n- name: Task 9: Create databases\n  mysql_db:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    state: present\n    login_user: root\n    login_password: "{{ mysql_root_password }}"\n    login_socket: "{{ mysql_socket }}"\n  with_items: "{{ mysql_databases }}"\n  when: mysql_databases is defined\n\n- name: Task 10: Create users\n  mysql_user:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    password: "{{ item.password }}"\n    priv: "{{ item.privileges }}"\n    login_user: root\n    login_password: "{{ mysql_root_password }}"\n    login_socket: "{{ mysql_socket }}"\n  with_items: "{{ mysql_users }}"\n  when: mysql_users is defined\n\n- name: Task 11: Flush handlers again\n  meta: flush_handlers\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-