her type. Looking at the playbook, the only place where a non-boolean is used is in the `notify` section, but that\'s a string, which is correct.\n\nWait, perhaps the `changed_when` is being set to a string instead of a boolean. Let me check: in the playbook, `changed_when: false` is correct. So why the error?\n\nWait, maybe the issue is that `changed_when` is expecting a boolean, but in the playbook, it\'s set to `false`, which is correct. So perhaps the linter is misconfigured or there\'s another issue.\n\nWait, perhaps the problem is not with `changed_when` but with another key. Let me look again at the error message: line 38, column 14. Let\'s count the lines in the playbook.\n\nThe playbook has:\n\n- Task 1: line 1-4\n- Task 2: line 5-6\n- Task 3: line 7-12\n- Task 4: line 13-14\n- Task 5: line 15-20\n- Task 6: line 21-23\n\nWait, perhaps the line numbers are off. Let me recount.\n\nWait, the user provided the faulty playbook, and the error is at line 38:14. That suggests the playbook is longer. Wait, perhaps I missed some tasks.\n\nWait, the original playbook has 6 tasks, but in the provided YAML, each task is on separate lines. Let me count the lines in the provided YAML:\n\nLine 1: ---\nLine 2: - name: Import assert.yml\nLine 3:   import_tasks: ../../assert.yml\nLine 4:   vars:\nLine 5:     ansible_run_once: true\nLine 6: \nLine 7: - name: Install nginx\nLine 8:   apt:\nLine 9:     name: nginx\nLine 10:     state: present\nLine 11: \nLine 12: - name: Place nginx.conf\nLine 13:   template:\nLine 14:     src: nginx.conf.j2\nLine 15:     dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\nLine 16:   notify: restart_nginx\nLine 17:   register: nginx_conf_result\nLine 18:   changed_when: false\nLine 19: \nLine 20: - name: Ensure /etc/nginx/conf.d exists\nLine 21:   file:\nLine 22:     path: /etc/nginx/conf.d\nLine 23:     state: directory\nLine 24:     mode: 0755\nLine 25: \nLine 26: - name: Place default.conf\nLine 27:   template:\nLine 28:     src: default.conf.j2\nLine 29:     dest: