abled\' to true. Also, use \'become\' for root access.\n\n7. **Schedule cron jobs**: Loop over \'cron_jobs\' and use the \'cron\' module for each job. Each job has a name, command, and optional parameters. The state defaults to \'present\' and user to the current user. I\'ll only run this task if \'cron_jobs\' is defined.\n\nI need to ensure that all tasks are in the correct order and that variables are properly referenced with double curly braces. Also, I\'ll make sure that each task has the correct modules and parameters as specified.\n\nI should also check for any potential issues, like variable undefined errors or incorrect module usage. For example, in Task 1, I\'m using \'import_tasks\' correctly, and in Tasks 3-5, I\'m handling the file modifications and handlers properly.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the playbook with each task as a YAML block under \'tasks\', ensuring proper indentation and no extra comments or explanations, as per the instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import the tasks defined in assert.yml\n  import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  remote_host: localhost\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Task 2: Install cron\n  become: yes\n  package:\n    name: "{{ cron_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure shell\n  become: yes\n  lineinfile:\n    path: "{{ cron_configuration }}"\n    line: "{{ cron_shell | backslashed }}"\n    mode: 0600\n    state: present\n  notify: Restart cron\n\n- name: Task 4: Configure path\n  become: yes\n  lineinfile:\n    path: "{{ cron_configuration }}"\n    line: "{{ cron_path | backslashed }}"\n    mode: 0600\n    state: present\n  notify: Restart cron\n\n- name: Task 5: Configure mailto\n  become: yes\n  lineinfile:\n    path: "{{ cron_configuration }}"\n    line: "{{ cron_mailto | backslashed }}"\n    mode: 0600\n    state: present\n  notify: Restart cron\n\n- name: Task 6: Start and enable cron\n  become: yes\n  service:\n    name: "{{ cron_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when: cron_service is defined and cron_service != ""\n\n- name: Task 7: Schedule requested cron jobs\n  become: yes\n  cron:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    command: "{{ item.job_command }}"\n    minute: "{{ item minute | default(\'*/5\') }}"\n    hour: "{{ item.hour | default(\'*\') }}"\n    day: "{{ item.day | default(\'*\') }}"\n    month: "{{ item.month | default(\'*\') }}"\n    weekday: "{{ item.weekday | default(\'*\') }}"\n    special_time: "{{ item.special_time | default(\'\') }}"\n    state: "{{ item.state | default(\'present\') }}"\n    user: "{{ item.user | default(\'root\') }}"\n  loop: "{{ cron_jobs | default([]) }}"\n  when: cron_jobs is defined\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-15T15:59:25.3122994Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 21311596192, 'load_duration': 85434877, 'prompt_eval_count': 777, 'prompt_eval_duration': 377560974, 'eval_count': 1109, 'eval_duration': 20847834478, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--6fd8b727-0f37-44d4-bf55-619c0fce79ba-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 777, 'output_tokens': 1109, 'total_tokens': 1886}
