sk with the appropriate \'name\', \'ansible.\' module, and any necessary parameters. For the conditional tasks, I\'ll use \'when\' for Task 1 and \'only_if\' for Task 4 to control execution.\n\nFinally, I\'ll ensure that the playbook starts with \'---\' followed by the tasks, properly indented and formatted according to YAML standards. No explanations or comments should be included, just the YAML code.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install epel\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: epel-release\n    state: present\n    when: ansible_distribution in [\'amzn2\', \'redhat\', \'centos\'] and ansible_major_version in [\'7\', \'8\', \'9\', \'10\']\n\n- name: Install epel gpg key\n  ansible.builtin.rpm_key:\n    key: "{{ epel_gpg_key }}"\n\n- name: Install epel-release\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: "{{ epel_url }}"\n    state: present\n    notify: Update package cache\n\n- name: Install epel-next-release\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: "{{ epel_next_url }}"\n    state: present\n    only_if: epel_next | bool\n    notify: Update package cache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-15T16:16:02.471006943Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16454677795, 'load_duration': 77262621, 'prompt_eval_count': 464, 'prompt_eval_duration': 146324479, 'eval_count': 728, 'eval_duration': 16230237068, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--d0ebed8a-6b9e-4403-80e1-920c06bcfabe-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 464, 'output_tokens': 728, 'total_tokens': 1192}
